// Depth only, from the camera's point of view.
//
// **The vertex stage is pbr.rvshader's, include for include, and that is the
// whole design.** A prepass is only useful if the depth it writes is the depth
// the lit pass would have written; if the two stages reach gl_Position by
// different routes the optimiser is free to fold them differently, the values
// disagree in the last bit, and a LessOrEqual test then drops scattered
// fragments of every surface -- which reads as speckled holes in the model and
// not as a depth bug. Sharing the source makes that impossible rather than
// unlikely.
//
// The fragment stage writes nothing, exactly as shadow_depth.rvshader's does:
// depth is written by the fixed-function stage, and a stage with no output and
// no discard is what lets the hardware reject a hidden fragment before it runs
// at all -- which is the entire point of the pass.
//
// The varyings scene_vertex.glsl declares go unread here. That is allowed and
// costs a little vertex bandwidth; the alternative is a second copy of the
// vertex stage, which is the one thing this file must not have.
#type vertex
#version 450 core

#include "include/scene_vertex.glsl"
#include "include/static_vertex.glsl"

#type fragment
#version 450 core

void main()
{
}
